  detailed_description: 'WC-Co cemented carbide (hardmetal) is the most important hard material in metallography. WC grain size per ASTM B390, porosity per ASTM B276, and Co binder distribution are the primary analysis targets. Diamond preparation is mandatory at all stages.',
